>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Split`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.Split : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a split rule for use in one extension simplifier call.

Passing `Split th` in the theorem list of a `simpExtLib` simplification
tactic adds `th` as a split looper for that call, as
`simpExtLib.add_split th` does. A rule that is not a split rule is ignored
with a warning.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss
     [simpExtLib.Split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)]
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”)
     (Context.snapshot());
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.add_split`](#simpExtLib.add_split),
[`splitLib.SPLIT_TAC`](#splitLib.SPLIT_TAC),
[`simpExtLib.ExclX`](#simpExtLib.ExclX).
